{{en-adj|farther,further|sup=+,farthermost,furthermost}}

# {{senseid|en|distant}} [[distant|Distant]]; remote in space.
#: {{ux|en|He went to a '''far''' land.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Joshua|9|6|passage=And they went to Ioshua vnto the campe at Gilgal, and said vnto him, and to the men of Israel, Wee be come from a '''farre''' countrey: Now therefore make ye a league with vs.}}
# Remote in time.
#: ''the '''far far''' future''
# Long. {{rfex|en}}
# More remote of two.
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=19|passage=At the '''far''' end of the houses the head gardener stood waiting for his mistress, and he gave her strips of bass to tie up her nosegay. This she did slowly and laboriously, with knuckly old fingers that shook.}}
#: {{ux|en|See those two mountains? The ogre lives on the '''far''' one.}}
#: {{ux|en|He moved to the '''far''' end of the state. She remained at this end.}}
# Extreme, as measured from some central or neutral position.
#: {{ux|en|They are on the '''far''' right on this issue.}}
# [[extreme|Extreme]], as a difference in nature or quality.
# {{lb|en|programming|not comparable}} Outside the currently selected [[segment]] in a segmented [[memory]] [[architecture]].
#: {{ux|en|'''far''' heap; '''far''' memory; '''far''' pointer}}

=====Usage notes=====
Comparable senses often repeat the adjective to intensify the meaning rather than using ''very'' as most other adjectives do. For example, one may speak of the {{good||'''far far future'''}} rather than the {{qmark||''very far future''}}.

